#
# Conformance case: validation/reifier-shape
# Proves the validation-shape PROJECTION for the RDF-1.2 STATEMENT-LAYER reifier
# obligation family: the closed-world condition "every K→P→value assertion must be
# reified, and its reifier must conform to shape C", authored in the classic RDF
# reification form (rdf:Statement + rdf:subject/rdf:predicate + a typed reifier). It
# lowers to a property shape on P carrying sh:reifierShape {C}-shape +
# sh:reificationRequired true. ShEx has no statement layer, so the reifier condition
# is carried in the canonical logic: layer (a ShEx-only residue row).

@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
@prefix g:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/provenance/> .

# The reifier's shape C (g:Endorsement): constrained by FAMILY 1 so the {C}-shape
# node the sh:reifierShape reference resolves to genuinely exists — an endorsement's
# endorsedBy values are agents (allValuesFrom g:Agent → sh:class g:Agent).
g:Agent a owl:Class .
g:Endorsement a owl:Class ;
    rdfs:subClassOf [
        a owl:Restriction ;
        owl:onProperty g:endorsedBy ;
        owl:allValuesFrom g:Agent
    ] .

# The obligation subject K (g:Record).
g:Record a owl:Class .

g:asserts    a owl:ObjectProperty .
g:endorsedBy a owl:ObjectProperty .

# The statement-layer reifier obligation: every g:Record g:asserts value must be
# reified by a g:Endorsement. Authored as a classic rdf:Statement whose reifier is
# typed g:Endorsement (the shape C) — no logic: scope, so it is inert to the logic
# frontend and read only by the shape derivation (FAMILY 5).
[] a rdf:Statement, g:Endorsement ;
    rdf:subject g:Record ;
    rdf:predicate g:asserts .
